      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Module 4: Integrated circuit design\n",
        "\n",
        "In this section you will work on your fourth module task. As you did before, please ensure that you are working in your own copy of the notebook and you have successfully run all the cells above.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this task, we will take the HDL description of the 32-bit counter and use OpenLane EDA tools to produce a physical layout for it.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "**What you need to do**\n",
        "\n",
        "Firstly, set up Nix, OpenLane2 and SKY130 Open PDK in your Colab runtime environment, and then action the following steps:\n",
        "1. Write the design file and install utility function.\n",
        "1. Import the SKY130 PDK and start logic synthesis.\n",
        "1. Action the logic synthesiser.\n",
        "1. Complete floorplanning and PDN generation.\n",
        "1. Place the design.\n",
        "1. Route the clock tree and the design.\n",
        "1. Sign-off and tape-out.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "The following sections contain the code you need to complete these steps. Follow the boxes one by one.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Hd6x1cL5yTzq"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "26oh0OKYy0eE"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Write the design file\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the following code to create a verilog file for the 32-bit counter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "%%writefile /content/counter32.v\n",
        "/**\n",
        " * 32-Bit Binary Counter\n",
        " *\n",
        " * This module implements a basic up-counter that increments on the\n",
        " * positive edge of the clock (clk) when the enable signal (en) is high.\n",
        " * An asynchronous, active-high reset (reset) to initialise the count to 0.\n",
        " *\n",
        " * Inputs:\n",
        " * clk   : System clock signal.\n",
        " * reset : Asynchronous reset (active high).\n",
        " * en    : Enable signal for counting (active high).\n",
        " *\n",
        " * Output:\n",
        " * count : 32-bit register holding the current count value.\n",
        " */\n",
        "module counter32 (\n",
        "    input wire clk,\n",
        "    input wire reset,\n",
        "    input wire en,\n",
        "    output reg [31:0] count\n",
        ");\n",
        "\n",
        "// The 'always' block is sensitive to the positive edge of the clock (posedge clk)\n",
        "// and the positive edge of the reset (posedge reset) for asynchronous reset handling.\n",
        "always @(posedge clk or posedge reset) begin\n",
        "    if (reset) begin\n",
        "        // Asynchronous reset: Immediately sets the counter to zero\n",
        "        count <= 32'h0;\n",
        "    end else if (en) begin\n",
        "        // Synchronous increment: Increments the count on the positive edge of clk\n",
        "        // if the enable signal is active (en = 1).\n",
        "        count <= count + 1;\n",
        "    end\n",
        "    // If 'en' is low, the count holds its current value\n",
        "end\n",
        "\n",
        "endmodule"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tOi1a-oxrjg7"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run the next box to install a utility function for better pictures."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SMv1ez1MVN52"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "%%writefile /content/openlane_ipynb/openlane/scripts/klayout/render.py\n",
        "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n",
        "# @markdown This makes ``display()`` to generate image of a higher resolution (default: 2500 pixels).\n",
        "# More information about layers can be found at this\n",
        "# [link](https://skywater-pdk.readthedocs.io/en/main/rules/layers.html). To hide the layer in the output image, comment off from the list.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Copyright (c) 2021-2022 Efabless Corporation\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n",
        "# you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n",
        "# You may obtain a copy of the License at\n",
        "#\n",
        "#      http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n",
        "# distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n",
        "# WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n",
        "# See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n",
        "# limitations under the License.\n",
        "\n",
        "from typing import Tuple\n",
        "import pya\n",
        "import click\n",
        "@click.command()\n",
        "@click.option(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True)\n",
        "@click.option(\"-l\", \"--input-lef\", \"input_lefs\", multiple=True,)\n",
        "@click.option( \"-T\", \"--lyt\", required=True, help=\"KLayout .lyt file\",)\n",
        "@click.option( \"-P\", \"--lyp\", required=True, help=\"KLayout .lyp file\",)\n",
        "@click.option( \"-M\", \"--lym\", required=True, help=\"KLayout .map (LEF/DEF layer map) file\",)\n",
        "@click.argument(\"input\")\n",
        "def render(input_lefs: Tuple[str, ...], output: str, lyt: str, lyp: str, lym: str, input: str,):\n",
        "    image_res = 2500 # @param {key:\"image resolution\", type:\"number\"}\n",
        "    # display ONLY the layers in the following list\n",
        "    selected_layers = [\n",
        "        \"diff.\",\n",
        "        \"dnwell.\",\n",
        "        \"li1.\",\n",
        "        \"licon1.\",\n",
        "        \"mcon.\",\n",
        "        \"met1.\",\n",
        "        \"met2.\",\n",
        "        \"met3.\",\n",
        "        \"met4.\",\n",
        "        \"met5.\",\n",
        "        #\"vnpc.\",\n",
        "        #\"vnsdm.\",\n",
        "        #\"vnwell.\",\n",
        "        \"poly.\",\n",
        "        \"psdm.\",\n",
        "        \"pwell.\",\n",
        "        \"tap.\",\n",
        "        \"via.\",\n",
        "        \"via2.\",\n",
        "        \"via3.\",\n",
        "        \"via4.\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        gds = input.endswith(\".gds\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Load technology file\n",
        "        tech = pya.Technology()\n",
        "        tech.load(lyt)\n",
        "\n",
        "        layout_options = None\n",
        "        if not gds:\n",
        "            layout_options = tech.load_layout_options\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.map_file = lym\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.macro_resolution_mode = 1\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.read_lef_with_def = False\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.lef_files = list(input_lefs)\n",
        "\n",
        "        view = pya.LayoutView()\n",
        "        view.load_layer_props(lyp)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if gds:\n",
        "            view.load_layout(input)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            view.load_layout(input, layout_options, lyt)\n",
        "\n",
        "        view.max_hier()\n",
        "\n",
        "        # control the visibility of the layers\n",
        "        for layer in view.each_layer():\n",
        "            layer.visible = False\n",
        "            if '122/16@1' in layer.source: # grid and ruler\n",
        "                layer.visible = True\n",
        "            for t in selected_layers:\n",
        "                if t in layer.name:\n",
        "                    layer.visible = True\n",
        "\n",
        "        pixels = view.get_pixels_with_options(image_res, image_res)\n",
        "\n",
        "        with open(output, \"wb\") as f:\n",
        "            f.write(pixels.to_png_data())\n",
        "\n",
        "        # save an image of larger resolution\n",
        "        pixels = view.get_pixels_with_options(image_res, image_res)\n",
        "        with open(\"/content/openlane_run/output.png\", \"wb\") as f:\n",
        "            f.write(pixels.to_png_data())\n",
        "\n",
        "    except Exception as e:\n",
        "        print(e)\n",
        "        exit(1)\n",
        "\n",
        "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n",
        "    render()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "cellView": "form",
        "id": "aVfYwP4JVLVy"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Import SKY130 PDK\n",
        "\n",
        "The OpenLane software will be controlled using a Python programme which will be listed below. The first snippet imports the OpenLane libraries and sets up the use of SKY130 PDK for our design ``counter32.v``."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "m8XFGVtbTwDI"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hmEi1Dq7y0eG"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from openlane.steps import Step\n",
        "from openlane.state import State\n",
        "from openlane.config import Config\n",
        "\n",
        "Config.interactive(\n",
        "    \"counter32\",\n",
        "    PDK=\"sky130A\",\n",
        "    CLOCK_PORT=\"clk\",\n",
        "    CLOCK_NET=\"clk\",\n",
        "    CLOCK_PERIOD=10,\n",
        "    GPL_CELL_PADDING=2,\n",
        "    DPL_CELL_PADDING=2,\n",
        "    PRIMARY_GDSII_STREAMOUT_TOOL=\"klayout\",\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "There will be a long list of text mentioning the set of files loaded from the PDK."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0rDOvPuJW3z6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ko4pxeMNymHc"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Logic synthesis\n",
        "\n",
        "Yosys is the logic synthesiser in OpenLane. The following code creates a Synthesis object and asks the logic synthesiser to work on the counter design.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Synthesis = Step.factory.get(\"Yosys.Synthesis\")\n",
        "synthesis = Synthesis(\n",
        "    VERILOG_FILES=[\"/content/counter32.v\"],\n",
        "    state_in=State(),\n",
        ")\n",
        "synthesis.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "huDcSylsjyMF"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Look at the statistics near the end. Which cell is used most in the mapping?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Note the chip area at this stage.\n",
        "\n",
        "Chip area = *Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KcYnEkMjX_Qe"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Floorplanning\n",
        "\n",
        "The key tasks are to set the size of the die and create the vital power distribution network."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zD_Wpah6aEbV"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Floorplan = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.Floorplan\")\n",
        "floorplan = Floorplan(state_in=synthesis.state_out)\n",
        "floorplan.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "szzGmo4qks2h"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Look for die area in the log. What is the die area? How many rows of standard cell sites are allocated?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ieum9A0T0sWx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run the code in the next box."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9fwykSNP0Trb"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "TapEndcapInsertion = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.TapEndcapInsertion\")\n",
        "tdi = TapEndcapInsertion(state_in=floorplan.state_out)\n",
        "tdi.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "IOPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.IOPlacement\")\n",
        "ioplace = IOPlacement(state_in=tdi.state_out)\n",
        "ioplace.start()\n",
        "display(ioplace)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "neEweF5jk1Sj"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "What difference did you notice?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SjTsY8mW0XLn"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# generate power distribution network (PDN)\n",
        "GeneratePDN = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GeneratePDN\")\n",
        "pdn = GeneratePDN(\n",
        "    state_in=ioplace.state_out,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_AUTO_ADJUST=True,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_VPITCH=25,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_HPITCH=25,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_VOFFSET=5,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_HOFFSET=5,\n",
        ")\n",
        "pdn.start()\n",
        "display(pdn)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PdfKKP1slUrE"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Which metal layers are used for the PDN? Suggest a reason.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Vujriy3_0Aiu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 5: Placement\n",
        "\n",
        "The iterative global and detailed placements confirms the phyical positions of the standard cells."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BboCoGltblXM"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Global placement\n",
        "GlobalPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GlobalPlacement\")\n",
        "gpl = GlobalPlacement(state_in=pdn.state_out)\n",
        "gpl.start()\n",
        "display(gpl)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "i_R4JVzEmlrb"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "How many iterations (``Iter``) did the placer spend? What has changed along the iterations?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Do you notice the overlapping of the cells? Why would that be the case?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f0Xef30cty48"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# run detailed placement\n",
        "DetailedPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.DetailedPlacement\")\n",
        "dpl = DetailedPlacement(state_in=gpl.state_out)\n",
        "dpl.start()\n",
        "display(dpl)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "74p8RBQ2mz60"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Looking through the log, what is the percentage change in the half-perimeter wirelength (HPWL)?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Compare the total cell area with the one at the end of logic synthesis. How much more area is used?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "r42aphRNup8S"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 6: Routing\n",
        "\n",
        "The counter has a clock signal that runs to the flip-flops. Ahead of the global routing and detailed routing, the clock tree is synthesised. In the end, the whole design is fully routed."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "izitoT5cbpTv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# clock tree synthesis\n",
        "CTS = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.CTS\")\n",
        "cts = CTS(state_in=dpl.state_out)\n",
        "cts.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Lf97TpcBkB6A"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "How many clock buffers has been added? What is the purpose of clock buffer?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NFEkpBcxvQWP"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Global routing\n",
        "GlobalRouting = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GlobalRouting\")\n",
        "grt = GlobalRouting(state_in=cts.state_out)\n",
        "grt.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fQ7WOrtgnAzR"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "What is the total wirelength? How many nets are routed?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "27cD7DOgihYs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "DetailedRouting = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.DetailedRouting\")\n",
        "drt = DetailedRouting(state_in=grt.state_out)\n",
        "drt.start()\n",
        "display(drt)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GbDfKl2TnOMn"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Inspect the log and the routed design. How many optimisation iterations were used? What would be the main objective in these iterations?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JWVgqlcxzgaG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 7: Sign-off\n",
        "\n",
        "The final touches to make sure the layout is correct and manufacturable."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b1VZa0l5cxw7"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Run fill insertion and display\n",
        "FillInsertion = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.FillInsertion\")\n",
        "fill = FillInsertion(state_in=drt.state_out)\n",
        "fill.start()\n",
        "display(fill)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iTsdRjn5nX7V"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Describe the main difference on the layout after fill insertion.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ViSiUD3_wCjl"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we will extract parasitic RC from the layout and run the static timing analysis (STA)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Z3DpsgyzwJAA"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "RCX = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.RCX\")\n",
        "rcx = RCX(state_in=fill.state_out)\n",
        "rcx.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "STAPostPNR = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.STAPostPNR\")\n",
        "sta_post_pnr = STAPostPNR(state_in=rcx.state_out)\n",
        "sta_post_pnr.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VVjBr2uXnXr_"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Generate the final GDSII layout\n",
        "StreamOut = Step.factory.get(\"KLayout.StreamOut\")\n",
        "gds = StreamOut(state_in=sta_post_pnr.state_out)\n",
        "gds.start()\n",
        "display(gds)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "F6NaVjrUnpHr"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Please save a copy of the picture of this final layout for your final assignment."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-Ke3HEESw1xX"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Final design rule check\n",
        "DRC = Step.factory.get(\"Magic.DRC\")\n",
        "drc = DRC(state_in=gds.state_out)\n",
        "drc.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SJfEOwxnnypY"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Is there any DRC? (Yes/No)\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "C4tAMzaQw_4t"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# extract the SPICE netlist of devices and connections from the layout\n",
        "SpiceExtraction = Step.factory.get(\"Magic.SpiceExtraction\")\n",
        "spx = SpiceExtraction(state_in=drc.state_out)\n",
        "spx.start()\n",
        "# Run layout-vs-schematic (LVS)\n",
        "LVS = Step.factory.get(\"Netgen.LVS\")\n",
        "lvs = LVS(state_in=spx.state_out)\n",
        "lvs.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6-aalCSzn3sQ"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Does the layout match with the schematic? (Yes/No)\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "If your answer is **YES**, then the layout is ready for a tape-out to the foundry! That's the end of the EDA journey."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "g7zujk_QxJ44"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "**What did I learn?**\n",
        "\n",
        "When you have completed the generation of a physical layout of a 32-bit counter, add your thoughts in response to the following question. You will want to keep these, as you will find them useful when working on later modules and your final assignment. To get started, double click this cell and edit the text.\n",
        "\n",
