    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "You have now reached the end of the notebook for this week. Please return to Canvas to complete the rest of the work in module 4.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will resume our work in this notebook next week, when we will be working through Module 5: Assembly, testing and packaging."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qOoaCA87bKah"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Module 5: Assembly, testing and packaging\n",
        "In this section you will work on your fifth module task. Before attempting it, please ensure that you are working in your own copy of the notebook and you have successfully run all the cells above.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this task, we are going to prepare an inverter design for assembly and packaging using the popular wire bonding technology.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "**What you need to do**\n",
        "\n",
        "Firstly, set up Nix, OpenLane2 and SKY130 Open PDK in your Colab runtime environment, and then action the following steps:\n",
        "1. Write the design file and install the utility function.\n",
        "1. Run automatic floorplanning.\n",
        "1. Run manual floorplanning with fixed die size.\n",
        "1. Work out the expected die size with I/O pads inserted.\n",
        "\n",
        "The following sections contain the code and packages you need to complete these steps."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "00EJ4jFYa7xz"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1jS_6zecXg34"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Write the design file\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the following code to create a verilog file for a 32-bit inverter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "%%writefile /content/inverter32.v\n",
        "module inverter32 (\n",
        "    input  wire [31:0] a_in,\n",
        "    output wire [31:0] y_out\n",
        ");\n",
        "\n",
        "    assign y_out = ~a_in;\n",
        "endmodule"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "duK35NiUYy2Q"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run the next box to install a utility function to visualise the layout."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FE7NEmW8ZeBm"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "%%writefile /content/openlane_ipynb/openlane/scripts/klayout/render.py\n",
        "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n",
        "# @markdown This makes ``display()`` to generate image of a higher resolution. Only the metal layers are shown (others are hidden in this task).\n",
        "# More information about layers can be found at this\n",
        "# [link](https://skywater-pdk.readthedocs.io/en/main/rules/layers.html). To hide the layer in the output image, comment off from the list.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Copyright (c) 2021-2022 Efabless Corporation\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n",
        "# you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n",
        "# You may obtain a copy of the License at\n",
        "#\n",
        "#      http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n",
        "# distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n",
        "# WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n",
        "# See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n",
        "# limitations under the License.\n",
        "\n",
        "from typing import Tuple\n",
        "import pya\n",
        "import click\n",
        "@click.command()\n",
        "@click.option(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True)\n",
        "@click.option(\"-l\", \"--input-lef\", \"input_lefs\", multiple=True,)\n",
        "@click.option( \"-T\", \"--lyt\", required=True, help=\"KLayout .lyt file\",)\n",
        "@click.option( \"-P\", \"--lyp\", required=True, help=\"KLayout .lyp file\",)\n",
        "@click.option( \"-M\", \"--lym\", required=True, help=\"KLayout .map (LEF/DEF layer map) file\",)\n",
        "@click.argument(\"input\")\n",
        "def render(input_lefs: Tuple[str, ...], output: str, lyt: str, lyp: str, lym: str, input: str,):\n",
        "    image_res = 1000 # @param {key:\"image resolution\", type:\"number\"}\n",
        "    # display ONLY the layers in the following list\n",
        "    selected_layers = [\n",
        "        #\"diff.\",\n",
        "        #\"dnwell.\",\n",
        "        #\"li1.\",\n",
        "        #\"licon1.\",\n",
        "        #\"mcon.\",\n",
        "        \"met1.\",\n",
        "        \"met2.\",\n",
        "        \"met3.\",\n",
        "        \"met4.\",\n",
        "        \"met5.\",\n",
        "        #\"vnpc.\",\n",
        "        #\"vnsdm.\",\n",
        "        #\"vnwell.\",\n",
        "        #\"poly.\",\n",
        "        #\"psdm.\",\n",
        "        #\"pwell.\",\n",
        "        #\"tap.\",\n",
        "        \"via.\",\n",
        "        \"via2.\",\n",
        "        \"via3.\",\n",
        "        \"via4.\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        gds = input.endswith(\".gds\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Load technology file\n",
        "        tech = pya.Technology()\n",
        "        tech.load(lyt)\n",
        "\n",
        "        layout_options = None\n",
        "        if not gds:\n",
        "            layout_options = tech.load_layout_options\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.map_file = lym\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.macro_resolution_mode = 1\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.read_lef_with_def = False\n",
        "            layout_options.lefdef_config.lef_files = list(input_lefs)\n",
        "\n",
        "        view = pya.LayoutView()\n",
        "        view.load_layer_props(lyp)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if gds:\n",
        "            view.load_layout(input)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            view.load_layout(input, layout_options, lyt)\n",
        "\n",
        "        view.max_hier()\n",
        "\n",
        "        # control the visibility of the layers\n",
        "        for layer in view.each_layer():\n",
        "            layer.visible = False\n",
        "            if '122/16@1' in layer.source: # grid and ruler\n",
        "                layer.visible = True\n",
        "            for t in selected_layers:\n",
        "                if t in layer.name:\n",
        "                    layer.visible = True\n",
        "\n",
        "        pixels = view.get_pixels_with_options(image_res, image_res)\n",
        "\n",
        "        with open(output, \"wb\") as f:\n",
        "            f.write(pixels.to_png_data())\n",
        "\n",
        "        # save an image of larger resolution\n",
        "        pixels = view.get_pixels_with_options(image_res, image_res)\n",
        "        with open(\"/content/openlane_run/output.png\", \"wb\") as f:\n",
        "            f.write(pixels.to_png_data())\n",
        "\n",
        "    except Exception as e:\n",
        "        print(e)\n",
        "        exit(1)\n",
        "\n",
        "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n",
        "    render()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "cellView": "form",
        "id": "zb_05l9EZeBp"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: First trial – automatic floorplan\n",
        "\n",
        "We will set up OpenLane as usual, taking all default settings."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jrcQVCgiZeBq"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "l_HUD-nkZeBr"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from openlane.steps import Step\n",
        "from openlane.state import State\n",
        "from openlane.config import Config\n",
        "\n",
        "Config.interactive(\n",
        "    \"inverter32\",\n",
        "    PDK=\"sky130A\",\n",
        "    PRIMARY_GDSII_STREAMOUT_TOOL=\"klayout\",\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we will synthesise the circuit."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "p_lld_9MZeBr"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Synthesis = Step.factory.get(\"Yosys.Synthesis\")\n",
        "synthesis = Synthesis(\n",
        "    VERILOG_FILES=[\"/content/inverter32.v\"],\n",
        "    state_in=State(),\n",
        ")\n",
        "synthesis.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zJ2_LRmjZeBr"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "As we expected, there are 32 inverter standard cells. How many public wires and public wire bits are there? Can you guess their meaning?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pHd8pDB1ZeBr"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we will proceed with floorplanning. Remember that the tool is set to find the smallest possible size of the die."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "psyr_kiYZeBr"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Floorplan = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.Floorplan\")\n",
        "floorplan = Floorplan(state_in=synthesis.state_out)\n",
        "floorplan.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OmbAbQPFZeBs"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Look for die area in the log. What is the dimension of the die?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4wZMGXWvZeBs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we will insert tap cells and end cap cells. Then randomly assign I/O pins."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bctm0CUWZeBs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "TapEndcapInsertion = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.TapEndcapInsertion\")\n",
        "tdi = TapEndcapInsertion(state_in=floorplan.state_out)\n",
        "tdi.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "IOPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.IOPlacement\")\n",
        "ioplace = IOPlacement(state_in=tdi.state_out)\n",
        "ioplace.start()\n",
        "display(ioplace)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "oY73IgUoZeBs"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "You should receive an error at this box. What is the explanation of the **ERROR** from the floorplan?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gCK1YcwfwxhQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Second trial – floorplan with fixed die size\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on the suggestion from the tools, provide a new dimension for the die to fit all I/O pins. Enter your answers (new width, new height) in the form below.\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qRf40azZevKV"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "u3mwEHTteuXh"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from openlane.steps import Step\n",
        "from openlane.state import State\n",
        "from openlane.config import Config\n",
        "\n",
        "new_die_width = 10 # @param {key:\"New die width\", type:\"number\"}\n",
        "new_die_height = 10 # @param {key:\"New die height\", type:\"number\"}\n",
        "Config.interactive(\n",
        "    \"inverter32\",\n",
        "    PDK=\"sky130A\",\n",
        "    DIE_AREA=[0, 0, new_die_width, new_die_height],\n",
        "    PRIMARY_GDSII_STREAMOUT_TOOL=\"klayout\",\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Let's synthesise again."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tbSf9E-9yGfH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Synthesis = Step.factory.get(\"Yosys.Synthesis\")\n",
        "synthesis = Synthesis(\n",
        "    VERILOG_FILES=[\"/content/inverter32.v\"],\n",
        "    state_in=State(),\n",
        ")\n",
        "synthesis.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "419zwuSNyFff"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This time, we ask the floorplanner to respect the die size supplied with the option ``FP_SIZING`` as **absolute**. Run the floorplanning again."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fE2JMbIGyL5c"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Floorplan = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.Floorplan\")\n",
        "floorplan = Floorplan(FP_SIZING=\"absolute\", state_in=synthesis.state_out)\n",
        "floorplan.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7a3y0OI-lRQt"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Inspect the output on die area and confirm that the new dimension is in place.\n",
        "\n",
        "What is the core area in μm${}^2$?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Next, we will try again with the I/O placement."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AE11HZyEyd8j"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "TapEndcapInsertion = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.TapEndcapInsertion\")\n",
        "tdi = TapEndcapInsertion(state_in=floorplan.state_out)\n",
        "tdi.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "IOPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.IOPlacement\")\n",
        "ioplace = IOPlacement(state_in=tdi.state_out)\n",
        "ioplace.start()\n",
        "display(ioplace)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2c5ZaeQrmLDj"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If it is **not successful**, return to the first box in **Step 3** and enter a bigger width and height.\n",
        "\n",
        "Which metal layer(s) is/are used for the I/O pins?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Estimate the pitch of the I/O pins. The pitch is the distance between two pins.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iKayBNRMZeBs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We will proceed with the remaining steps of the physical implementation."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Cgco78c20COs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# generate power distribution network (PDN)\n",
        "GeneratePDN = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GeneratePDN\")\n",
        "pdn = GeneratePDN(\n",
        "    state_in=ioplace.state_out,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_AUTO_ADJUST=True,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_VPITCH=25,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_HPITCH=25,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_VOFFSET=5,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_HOFFSET=5,\n",
        ")\n",
        "pdn.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Global placement\n",
        "GlobalPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GlobalPlacement\")\n",
        "gpl = GlobalPlacement(state_in=pdn.state_out)\n",
        "gpl.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "# run detailed placement\n",
        "DetailedPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.DetailedPlacement\")\n",
        "dpl = DetailedPlacement(state_in=gpl.state_out)\n",
        "dpl.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "display(dpl)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TZGCiRqjZeBs"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we will route the design."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rMzEX4di0a2S"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Global routing\n",
        "GlobalRouting = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GlobalRouting\")\n",
        "grt = GlobalRouting(state_in=dpl.state_out)\n",
        "grt.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "DetailedRouting = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.DetailedRouting\")\n",
        "drt = DetailedRouting(state_in=grt.state_out)\n",
        "drt.start()\n",
        "display(drt)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QDT2NcQBZeBt"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Inspect the log and the routed design. What is the final total wirelength?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "You may consider this as the length required to connect the logic circuit with the I/O pins.\n",
        "\n",
        "Please save a copy of the picture of this final layout for your final assignment."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aE1_dsAnZeBt"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Challenges of inserting I/O pads"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Qh_PZIhc1xiH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "From the task above, we have successfully assigned I/O pins around the die, but without any I/O pads. I/O pads are necessary to provide electrical protection and an area for wire bonding.\n",
        "\n",
        "A typical in-line pad pitch required for 0.18 μm technology is [70 μm](https://www.onsemi.com/PowerSolutions/content.do?id=16679). What would be the dimension of the die if in-line pads are added?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "How many percentage of the area is used as the core in this case?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "B1dnpyQk1xiO"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "**What did I learn?**\n",
        "\n",
        "When you have completed the manual floorplanning to fit in I/O pins and pads, add your thoughts in response to the following question. You will want to keep these, as you will find them useful when working on later modules and your final assignment. To get started, double click this cell and edit the text.\n",
        "\n",
        "**How does assembly and packaging affect chip design? What are the necessary steps during design to prepare the chip for final packaging?**\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here.*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-G-yq-cdbYEH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "You have now reached the end of the notebook for this week. Please return to Canvas to complete the rest of the work in module 5.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "buU4AUavbdsE"
      }
    }
  ],
